    "user_name": "admiralbob77",
    "upload_extra": "a:10:{s:8:\"usertags\";s:36:\"electronic,rock,guitar,funky,hip_hop\";s:4:\"ccud\";s:43:\"media,remix,bpm_100_105,ccplus,how_i_did_it\";s:7:\"systags\";s:39:\"non_commercial,audio,mp3,44k,stereo,VBR\";s:3:\"bpm\";s:3:\"100\";s:12:\"relative_dir\";s:20:\"content/admiralbob77\";s:9:\"featuring\";s:7:\"apoxode\";s:6:\"ccplus\";b:1;s:4:\"nsfw\";b:0;s:9:\"howididit\";a:5:{s:5:\"tools\";s:98:\"A Korg NanoKey, a Yamaha P125 piano, an Alesis drum pad, GarageBand, Audacity, a Fender Telecaster\";s:7:\"samples\";s:110:\"apoxode posted a huge anthology mix of a whole pile of people, but it was cohesive and funky (in a swift way.)\";s:7:\"origial\";s:70:\"drum additions, a saw lead on the synth, an organ part, a guitar part.\";s:7:\"process\";s:345:\"I slowed the original down to 100 bpm and pitched it down from G to D. Then I cut it up a bit, and played a drum part between the cuts and in the quieter parts. It is a bit of a counter beat, tugging it to 100 BPM on the 1 when it doesn't necessarily want to be. \r\n\r\nI added the saw lead, and then filled in the holes with guitar and organ bits.\";s:5:\"other\";s:0:\"\";}s:11:\"num_reviews\";i:2;}",
